{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122224","id":4237716589,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc78lmxt","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122224","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122224.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122224.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122224","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122224/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122224/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122224/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/f36bc36cd958df3201711a08652952d30b357f4b","number":122224,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[Core]: Remove extra loads when using `compare_exchange_weak` in `SafeNumeric`","user":{"login":"NoctemCat","id":22471296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDcxMjk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22471296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat","html_url":"https://github.com/NoctemCat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nAcquire loads needs to be synchronized with concurrent release operations, which will make the code slower, so if we can remove extra loads in a hot path easily without changing the behaviour, we should remove them. \r\n\r\nThis PR removes them by lifting the first load acquire outside of the loop, as we only need it to load the initial current value. After that `compare_exchange_weak` will write the newest value into `expected` on failure with acquire memory ordering because we use a single `std::memory_order_acq_rel` argument. So in the next iteration we will have the newest value again.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nPer https://en.cppreference.com/cpp/atomic/atomic/compare_exchange `compare_exchange_weak` loads new data into `expected` on failure. See the last sentence.\r\n\r\n> Atomically compares the object representation of `*this` with that of `expected`. If those are bitwise-equal, replaces the former with `desired` (performs read-modify-write operation). Otherwise, **loads the actual value stored in `*this` into `expected`** (performs load operation).\r\n\r\nRelevant table snippet for the currently used overload, the operations in quote in the brackets `(performs * operation)` matches the operations in the columns:\r\n| read‑modify‑write operation | load operation |\r\n|  :---: |  :---: |\r\n| `order` | <ul><li>`std::memory_order_acquire` if `order` is `std::memory_order_acq_rel`</li><li>`std::memory_order_relaxed` if `order` is `std::memory_order_release`</li><li>otherwise `order`</li></ul>|\r\n\r\nI can also add `std::memory_order_acquire` into the argument for a memory order on failure directly to be more explicit if it is preferred.\r\n\r\n## Benchmark\r\n\r\nTests the worst case scenario, 8 threads modifying the same variable at the same time.\r\n\r\n```\r\nscons target=template_release optimize=speed accesskit=no use_llvm=yes linker=lld production=yes tests=yes\r\n```\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n\r\n<summary>Code</summary>\r\n\r\nModified from https://redirect.github.com/godotengine/godot-docs/pull/12200\r\n\r\n```c++\r\n\r\n#include \"core/os/semaphore.h\"\r\n#include \"core/os/thread.h\"\r\n#include \"tests/test_macros.h\"\r\n\r\n#include <algorithm>\r\n\r\nTEST_FORCE_LINK(test_user_bench)\r\n\r\n#include <chrono>\r\n#include <cstdio>\r\n\r\nconst int THREAD_NUMS = 8;\r\nconst uint64_t N = 800'000'000;\r\n\r\nstatic Semaphore thread_sem;\r\nstatic SafeNumeric<uint64_t> counter;\r\nstatic SafeFlag run_while_flag;\r\nstatic SafeFlag only_adds;\r\n\r\ndouble results[THREAD_NUMS];\r\n\r\nstruct ThreadData {\r\n\tuint64_t num_per_thread;\r\n\tuint32_t thread_idx;\r\n};\r\n\r\nstatic void thread_func(void *userdata) {\r\n\tThreadData data = *(ThreadData *)userdata;\r\n\tuint64_t num_per_thread = data.num_per_thread;\r\n\tuint32_t thread_idx = data.thread_idx;\r\n\r\n\tthread_sem.wait();\r\n\tauto t0 = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();\r\n\tfor (uint64_t i = 0; i < num_per_thread; i++) {\r\n\t\tcounter.conditional_increment();\r\n\t\tcounter.decrement();\r\n\t}\r\n\tauto t1 = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();\r\n\tresults[thread_idx] = std::chrono::duration<double, std::nano>(t1 - t0).count() / N;\r\n}\r\n\r\nstatic void thread_func_while(void *) {\r\n\tthread_sem.wait();\r\n\twhile (run_while_flag.is_set()) {\r\n\t\tif (only_adds.is_set()) {\r\n\t\t\tcounter.conditional_increment();\r\n\t\t\tcontinue;\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t\tif (counter.conditional_increment()) {\r\n\t\t\tcounter.decrement();\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n\r\nstatic void user_bench() {\r\n\tThread threads[THREAD_NUMS] = {};\r\n\r\n\t// --------- Speed ---------\r\n\tuint64_t num_per_thread = N / THREAD_NUMS;\r\n\tThreadData data[THREAD_NUMS] = {};\r\n\tfor (uint32_t i = 0; i < THREAD_NUMS; i++) {\r\n\t\tdata[i] = { num_per_thread, i };\r\n\t\tthreads[i].start(thread_func, data + i);\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\tcounter.set(1);\r\n\tthread_sem.post(THREAD_NUMS);\r\n\tfor (uint32_t i = 0; i < THREAD_NUMS; i++) {\r\n\t\tthreads[i].wait_to_finish();\r\n\t}\r\n\r\n\tdouble ns_per_op = *std::max_element(results, results + THREAD_NUMS);\r\n\tprintf(\"Benchmark result: %.1f ns/op (counter %zu)\\n\", ns_per_op, (size_t)counter.get());\r\n\tif (counter.get() != 1) {\r\n\t\tprintf(\"Should be 1 when in pairs.\");\r\n\t}\r\n\t// --------- Speed ---------\r\n\t\r\n\t// --------- Correctness ---------\r\n\tfor (uint32_t i = 0; i < THREAD_NUMS; i++) {\r\n\t\tthreads[i].start(thread_func_while, nullptr);\r\n\t}\r\n\tcounter.set(1);\r\n\trun_while_flag.set();\r\n\tonly_adds.clear();\r\n\tthread_sem.post(THREAD_NUMS);\r\n\tstd::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::microseconds(1000));\r\n\tuint64_t current_counter = counter.postdecrement();\r\n\tstd::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::microseconds(500));\r\n\tonly_adds.set();\r\n\tstd::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::microseconds(500));\r\n\trun_while_flag.clear();\r\n\r\n\tfor (uint32_t i = 0; i < THREAD_NUMS; i++) {\r\n\t\tthreads[i].wait_to_finish();\r\n\t}\r\n\tif (current_counter == 0) {\r\n\t\tprintf(\"Should never be 0 when valid.\");\r\n\t}\r\n\tif (counter.get() != 0) {\r\n\t\tprintf(\"Should be 0 after decrement.\");\r\n\t}\r\n\t// --------- Correctness ---------\r\n}\r\n\r\nREGISTER_TEST_COMMAND(\"user-bench\", &user_bench)\r\n```\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nI run it 2 times.\r\n| Run | PR | master |\r\n|  --- |  --- | --- |\r\n|  1   |  125.7 ns/op | 173.1 ns/op |\r\n| 2   | 112.0 ns/op | 174.0 ns/op |\r\n \r\nNo AI used\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nProvide additional information and explanation of your PR, including areas that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers. For examples, please read our pull request guidelines: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/pull_requests/pull_request_guidelines.html#explain-your-contributions\r\n-->\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","description":"","color":"447777","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","number":25,"state":"open","title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":343,"closed_issues":2335,"created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T06:28:22Z","closed_at":null,"due_on":null},"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-08-09T08:28:44Z","updated_at":"2026-08-11T00:50:31Z","closed_